## 0. Processes, one database

| Process | Entry | Serves |
| --- | --- | --- |
| API | `node dist/main.js`, `PORT` (<%= port %> in `.env.example`) | `/health/liveness`, `/health/readiness` |
<% if (consumer) { %>| consumer | `node dist/consumer.js` | no topic until a `consumer-handler` adds one; retrying on `arthome.<%= name %>.retry`, dead-lettering to `arthome.<%= name %>.dlq` |
<% } %><% if (sweeper) { %>| sweeper | `node dist/sweeper.js` | no pass yet |
<% } %>
**Stop every process before `migration:run`.** A migration may drop a column the running build still
reads.

Every process reads `DATABASE_URL` through `libs/config` (`NODE_ENV` required, never defaulted),
closes its pool on SIGTERM, and is booted as its entry point boots it by `src/boot.itest.ts`. The
API binds `@arthome-platform/http-edge`'s `edgeProviders` (`src/edge-providers.ts`); its readiness
fails only on the database, and the slot, the publication and the outbox retention answer
`degraded`.

Its connector is `infra/debezium/<%= name %>-outbox.json`, its topics are in `infra/kafka/topics.json`
(<%= topics.map((topic) => `\`arthome.${name}.${topic.aggregate}\``).join(', ') %>), and its database is in
`infra/postgres/init-databases.sql`, which runs only on an empty data directory: on a stack already
up, create the database by hand.

